-- title:
--   No macro class of monochromatic/unsaturated SAFE steps has all-target absorption (Astra's H_B theorem)
-- statement:
--   A tree witness $\theta$ defines a total order $\prec_\theta$ on $\mathbb Z$ (milestone framework). A finite word $W$ of integers is SAFE if, for some tree witness $\theta$, the sequence "letters of $W$, then all remaining integers in $\prec_\theta$-order" has no monotone 4-term AP. "Residue-complete" means it meets all four classes mod 4.
--
--   **Theorem (no macro class has all-target absorption).** Fix $B\in\mathbb N$. Let $\mathcal H$ be any class of SAFE, duplicate-free words such that every $W\in\mathcal H$ either (base) is not residue-complete or has $|W|\le B$, or (step) is $W=QR$ with $R\neq\emptyset$, $Q\in\mathcal H$, and either $R$ has a single parity, or $Q$ is not residue-complete and every suffix of $W$ after a residue-complete prefix has a single parity. Then no nonempty $\mathcal G\subseteq\mathcal H$ has the property that for every $Q\in\mathcal G$ and every $y\notin Q$ some end-extension $QR\in\mathcal G$ contains $y$.
--
--   This class contains GPT 6 Astra's macro class $\mathcal H_B$: start from $(0)$, then apply monochromatic steps, unsaturated mixed steps, or bounded whole-word exceptions $|W|\le B$. Astra's audit puts all current absorption recipes (restricted mod-8/mod-32 absorption, reflection blocks, the $H$ certificate, and so on) inside $\mathcal H_{12}$. So no invariant family generated by these recipes, or by any fixed finite set of bounded certificates added to them, can produce a 4-AP-free permutation of $\mathbb Z$. A successful construction needs an unbounded mixed-parity rule that applies after all four classes are present. Lemma of GPT 6 Astra.
-- source:
--   Erdős Problem 195 (https://www.erdosproblems.com/195); tree-witness framework; theorem of GPT 6 Astra; Lean-verified by Grok Bot for Ethan Cheung (Oct 23 2026)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_Erdos195_tree

namespace Erdos195

theorem macro_class_no_absorption (B : ℕ) (H G : List ℤ → Prop)
    (hH : ∀ W, H W → (∃ θ : ℕ → ℤ → Bool, Safe (treeLt θ) W) ∧ W.Nodup ∧
      ((¬ ∀ r : ℤ, ∃ x ∈ W, x % 4 = r % 4) ∨ W.length ≤ B ∨
       ∃ Q R : List ℤ, W = Q ++ R ∧ R ≠ [] ∧ H Q ∧
         ((∀ d ∈ R, ∀ d' ∈ R, d % 2 = d' % 2) ∨
          ((¬ ∀ r : ℤ, ∃ x ∈ Q, x % 4 = r % 4) ∧
            ∀ n : ℕ, (∀ r : ℤ, ∃ x ∈ W.take n, x % 4 = r % 4) →
              ∀ d ∈ W.drop n, ∀ d' ∈ W.drop n, d % 2 = d' % 2))))
    (hGH : ∀ W, G W → H W) (hne : ∃ W, G W) :
    ¬ ∀ Q, G Q → ∀ y : ℤ, y ∉ Q → ∃ R : List ℤ, G (Q ++ R) ∧ y ∈ Q ++ R := by sorry

end Erdos195
